<urn:adk-prov:runs/data/265dec56ceb5417f99d4560ba759d798> a lcont:LLMResponse ;
    dcterms:title "response:ProcessDescriptor_agent"^^xsd:string ;
    prov:value """```json
{
  "success": "This is a selective ketone reduction reaction converting ethyl 2-acetylhexanoate to ethyl 2-(1-hydroxyethyl)hexanoate through catalytic hydrogenation.\\n\\n**PROCESS OVERVIEW:**\\nThe reaction selectively reduces the ketone functional group (acetyl group) to a secondary alcohol while preserving the ester group. This is a hydrogenation process that requires precise control to avoid ester reduction.\\n\\n**KEY PROCESS PARAMETERS:**\\n- **Feedstock**: Ethyl 2-acetylhexanoate (186.25 g/mol) and hydrogen gas\\n- **Product**: Ethyl 2-(1-hydroxyethyl)hexanoate (188.26 g/mol)\\n- **Hydrogen Consumption**: 1 mole H2 per mole substrate (theoretical: 2.016 kg H2 per 186.25 kg substrate)\\n\\n**CATALYTIC SYSTEM:**\\n- **Catalysts**: Heterogeneous metal catalysts such as Ni/C, Pd/C, or Pt/C are typical choices\\n- **Alternative**: Homogeneous catalysts like RuCl2(PPh3)3 or RANEY nickel for enhanced selectivity\\n- **Catalyst Loading**: Typically 5-10 wt% for heterogeneous systems\\n\\n**REACTION CONDITIONS:**\\n- **Temperature**: 50-150°C (controlled to prevent side reactions)\\n- **Pressure**: 1-50 bar H2 (depending on catalyst activity and desired selectivity)\\n- **Solvent**: Protic solvents (ethanol, methanol) or aprotic solvents (ethyl acetate, THF) to facilitate mass transfer\\n- **Reaction Time**: 2-12 hours depending on temperature, pressure, and catalyst\\n\\n**SELECTIVITY CONSIDERATIONS:**\\n- The ketone is kinetically more reactive than the ester, enabling selective reduction\\n- Lower temperatures and milder pressures favor ketone selectivity over ester reduction\\n- Catalyst choice is critical: Pd/C shows excellent ketone selectivity; Ni/C may reduce esters under forcing conditions\\n\\n**EQUIPMENT:**\\n- Autoclave or pressure vessel rated for hydrogen (10-100 L typical scale)\\n- Gas-liquid contact system (stirred reactor with H2 sparger)\\n- Temperature control jacket\\n- Hydrogen supply system with pressure regulation and safety relief\\n- Catalyst filtration/separation equipment (if heterogeneous catalyst)\\n\\n**INDUSTRIAL SCALE-UP CONSIDERATIONS:**\\n- H2 consumption requires dedicated hydrogen infrastructure\\n- Safety systems for hydrogen management (explosion-proof equipment, inert atmosphere protocols)\\n- Product workup: catalyst removal (filtration), solvent recovery, potential vacuum distillation\\n- Typical yield: 90-98% under optimized conditions\\n- Atom economy: 97.8% (excellent)\\n\\n**WASTE/BYPRODUCTS:**\\n- Spent catalyst (requires regeneration or disposal)\\n- Solvent recovery necessary for economic viability\\n- Minimal waste with proper stoichiometric control"
}
```"""^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:adk-prov:runs/prompt/ProcessDescriptor_agent_process_completion_d41d8cd98f00b204> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:adk-prov:runs/process/50b893f774564fc38abdc5dcb3286f76> .

