<urn:adk-prov:runs/data/7ebd643701b748e5a9fd47e6d4da38a9> a lcont:LLMResponse ;
    dcterms:title "response:ProcessDescriptor_agent"^^xsd:string ;
    prov:value """```json
{
  "success": "This is an alkylation reaction, specifically a nucleophilic substitution (SN2) of ethyl acetoacetate with butyl bromide. This is a classic example of the acetoacetic ester synthesis, a fundamental organic synthetic procedure.\\n\\n**PROCESS DESCRIPTION:**\\n\\n**Reaction Type:** Alkylation via SN2 nucleophilic substitution\\n\\n**Chemical Overview:**\\nEthyl acetoacetate (β-ketoester) acts as a nucleophile through its active methylene group (CH2 between two electron-withdrawing carbonyls), attacking the primary alkyl halide (butyl bromide) to form a new C-C bond, displacing bromide as the leaving group.\\n\\n**Industrial/Laboratory Conditions:**\\n\\n**Base Catalyst:** Requires a strong base to deprotonate the active methylene:\\n- Sodium ethoxide (NaOEt) or potassium carbonate (K2CO3) in aprotic solvents\\n- Alternatively, sodium hydride (NaH) for enhanced reactivity\\n- Base: typically 1-2 molar equivalents\\n\\n**Solvent:** Polar aprotic solvents essential for SN2 reaction:\\n- Ethanol (if using NaOEt) or DMSO preferred\\n- N,N-Dimethylformamide (DMF) acceptable\\n- Avoids protic solvents that would solvate nucleophile excessively\\n\\n**Temperature:** Room temperature to 60-80°C\\n- Higher temperatures (50-80°C) accelerate reaction significantly\\n- Exothermic reaction requires controlled addition\\n\\n**Reaction Time:** 2-24 hours depending on temperature and base strength\\n\\n**Energy Requirements:**\\n- Moderate heat input for reflux conditions\\n- Exothermic process; cooling may be necessary during initial mixing\\n\\n**Equipment:**\\n- Round-bottom flask with stirring and reflux condenser\\n- Addition funnel for controlled alkyl halide addition\\n- Inert atmosphere (nitrogen/argon) recommended to exclude moisture\\n\\n**Scale-Up Considerations:**\\n- Exothermic nature requires careful temperature control at large scales\\n- Heat removal capacity critical\\n- SN2 reaction typically clean with minimal side products\\n- Workup involves acid quench and organic extraction\\n\\n**Product Yield:** Typically 60-85% under optimized conditions\\n\\n**Industrial Applications:** This acetoacetic ester alkylation is used to synthesize methyl ketones and other organic synthons in pharmaceutical and fine chemical manufacturing."
}
```"""^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:adk-prov:runs/prompt/ProcessDescriptor_agent_process_completion_d41d8cd98f00b204> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:adk-prov:runs/process/d3ac9b2a7fc24ade95ebc8a6d2add926> .

