    prov:value """```json
{
  "success": "This is a Knoevenagel condensation reaction between ethyl cyanoacetate and benzophenone to produce etocrylene (ethyl 2-cyano-3,3-diphenylprop-2-enoate), a UV-absorbing compound used in cosmetics and sunscreens.\\n\\n**PROCESS DESCRIPTION:**\\n\\n**Reaction Type:** Base-catalyzed Knoevenagel condensation (aldol-type reaction)\\n\\n**Key Process Parameters:**\\n\\n*Catalysts:* \\n- Primary: Weak organic bases (piperidine, pyrrolidine, or secondary amines) or inorganic bases (K2CO3, Cs2CO3, or NaOH at catalytic quantities)\\n- Alternative: DBU (1,8-diazabicyclo[5.4.0]undec-7-ene) or other organocatalysts\\n\\n*Solvents:*\\n- Polar aprotic solvents preferred: DMF, DMSO, or DMA (for faster reaction)\\n- Alternative: Methanol, ethanol, or toluene depending on scale and process economics\\n- Solvent choice affects reaction rate and product selectivity\\n\\n*Reaction Conditions:*\\n- Temperature: 25-80°C (room temperature to moderate heating)\\n- Pressure: Atmospheric to slightly elevated\\n- Duration: 2-24 hours depending on catalyst strength and temperature\\n- Stoichiometry: 1:1 molar ratio of ethyl cyanoacetate to benzophenone\\n\\n*Mechanism:*\\n1. Base abstracts α-hydrogen from ethyl cyanoacetate to form reactive carbanion\\n2. Carbanion attacks carbonyl carbon of benzophenone (electrophilic aromatic ketone)\\n3. Hydroxyl intermediate forms and undergoes dehydration to yield conjugated product\\n4. Water is the only stoichiometric byproduct (easily removed by azeotropic distillation or vacuum)\\n\\n**Industrial Considerations:**\\n\\n*Equipment:* Jacketed reactor with mechanical stirring, reflux condenser, thermometer, addition funnel for sequential mixing\\n\\n*Scale-up Factors:*\\n- Exothermic condensation; requires controlled temperature and cooling capacity\\n- Batch or semi-batch operation common in fine chemicals\\n- Heat removal critical to prevent decomposition\\n\\n*Workup & Purification:*\\n- Water removal by azeotropic distillation or vacuum distillation\\n- Product crystallization or column chromatography separation\\n- Final purification typically yields >95% pure etocrylene\\n\\n*Industrial Applications:* Etocrylene is a key intermediate/active ingredient in UV-absorbing cosmetic formulations (SPF products), with production ranging from kilograms to metric tons depending on demand.\\n\\n*Safety Notes:* Cyanoacetates are moderately toxic; proper ventilation and handling required. Exothermic nature requires temperature control to prevent runaway reactions."
}
```"""^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:adk-prov:runs/prompt/ProcessDescriptor_agent_process_completion_d41d8cd98f00b204> ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:adk-prov:runs/process/4270139cd419461eb0976f360f496d45> .

